------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled neuroimaging tools and model weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

medmcp-neuro-core wraps established third-party neuroimaging tools and
redistributes some of their pretrained weights/checkpoints (baked into the
published container image). Each remains under its own license and carries its
own citation requirements; if you use the results in research, please cite the
underlying methods (see the "Citation" section of README.md).

  - HD-BET (skull_strip) — brain extraction.
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/HD-BET
    Cite: Isensee et al., "Automated brain extraction of multi-sequence MRI
    using artificial neural networks", Human Brain Mapping (2019).
    doi:10.1002/hbm.24750

  - ANTs / ANTsPy (register_to_template, coregister, apply_transform) —
    image registration.
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/ANTsX/ANTsPy
    Cite: Tustison et al., "The ANTsX ecosystem for quantitative biological and
    medical imaging", Scientific Reports 11:9068 (2021).
    doi:10.1038/s41598-021-87564-6

  - FastSurfer (segment_brain) — deep-learning whole-brain segmentation
    (FastSurferVINN, seg-only; no FreeSurfer license required).
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/Deep-MI/FastSurfer
    Cite: Henschel et al., "FastSurfer - A fast and accurate deep learning based
    neuroimaging pipeline", NeuroImage 219:117012 (2020).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2020.117012
    Henschel et al., "FastSurferVINN: Building resolution-independence into deep
    learning segmentation methods", NeuroImage 251:118933 (2022).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2022.118933

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Standard-space templates
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - MNI152NLin2009cAsym (register_to_template default template), retrieved on
    first use from TemplateFlow and baked into the published container image.
    Distributed under the template's own license (see the LICENSE file in
    https://github.com/templateflow/tpl-MNI152NLin2009cAsym).
    Cite: Fonov et al., "Unbiased average age-appropriate atlases for pediatric
    studies", NeuroImage 54(1):313-327 (2011).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2010.07.033
    Retrieved via TemplateFlow: Ciric et al., "TemplateFlow: FAIR-sharing of
    multi-scale, multi-species brain models", Nature Methods 19:1568-1571 (2022).
    doi:10.1038/s41592-022-01681-2

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled libraries
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Python libraries redistributed inside the container image — including
PyTorch, nnU-Net (the engine HD-BET builds on), nibabel, and their transitive
dependency closure — each remain under their own license; the full license texts
travel with each package's distribution.
